# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- large, REGENERABLE artefacts -------------------------------------------------
# Excluded to keep the repo clonable, not because they do not matter. Each line says
# how to remake the thing, because "it is gitignored" and "it is lost" must not be the
# same sentence.

# 3D exports, 103 MB. Regenerate: JLC_LIB=<path> tools/export_3d.sh
# The STEP alone is 66 MB, over GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold.
cad/*.step
cad/*.glb
cad/tmp*.scad

# Historical board snapshots, 72 MB across 16 files. These are point-in-time copies
# taken before risky layout operations; git history now does that job properly.
.backup/

# SITL flight logs, 73 MB. Regenerate: bash sitl/run_scenarios.sh
sitl/logs/
sitl/terrain/*.DAT

# KiCad local state - per-user window layout and selection, not design data.
*.kicad_prl
_r.kicad_prl
_regress.kicad_prl
fp-info-cache

# KiCad backup written next to the board by an interrupted save.
*.kicad_pcb.bak

# Bench results are MEASUREMENTS of one physical board, not a property of the design.
# tools/check_rf.py deliberately fails until this exists; committing someone else's
# numbers would satisfy the gate without anyone having switched a board on.
fab/rf-bench-results.json

# ---- prose docs, held back until they are ready to publish --------------------------
# These are complete and used by the tooling locally; they are simply not polished
# enough to be the public face of the project yet. Delete these four lines to publish.
# docs/PARTS.csv and docs/img/ deliberately stay tracked: the CSV is DATA that
# gen_doc_tables.py and check_links.py read, and the renders are the project's photos.
docs/*.md

# Third-party datasheets, 5.6 MB. Cited by tools/check_thermal.py and fetchable from
# the manufacturers; no reason to redistribute them here.
docs/datasheets/

# OpenSCAD scratch file from a render run.
cad/tmp*.scad

# KiCad session lock and auto-backup directory.
*.lck
NAVCORE-SoOP-backups/

# Application notes, kept locally.
SPONSORSHIP.md

# Every markdown file except the top-level README is held back for now.
# They are all still on disk and the tooling reads them; they just aren't published.
cad/README.md
fab/ORDER.md
fab/README.md
sim/README.md
sitl/README.md
.scratch/
